WEBVTT

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.190
Well, shall we head to regionals?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:26.820
Uh huh!

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.530
You know it!

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.140
Let's get together...

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.980
After bickering with Kai,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.830
I didn't participate in any of the 
matches at the national tournament.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:36.390
The most frustrating thing about it is 
that we lost and I didn't do a thing...

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.630
This time, who cares about Kai?

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.050
I'm gonna pull this team to victory!

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.910
I'll tell you one thing. You won't beat me.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.530
Not with that deck.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.110
I'll get her back at the next nationals.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.100
I can't afford to lose at regionals!

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:12.570
I didn't win against Tetsu 
at the national tournament...

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.360
I once had fun in Vanguard 
fights, win or lose,

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.760
but after our match...

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.810
Instead, I felt despair, helplessness...

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:28.300
But then Kai made me remember 
my love for the fights.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.660
It's your fault.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.040
You can't beat them yet, 
not with your skill...

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.180
You mean I can get stronger?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.180
I wanna get stronger...

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.800
My frustration at losing 
will make me stronger.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.480
That's right. Nothing is a waste.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.970
At the training camp with Team Caesar, 
I learned how deep Vanguard is.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.810
Since then, I've loved it even more.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.390
Just from that, I feel 
like I've become stronger.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.310
Not to mention, that time...

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.510
It felt like the cards were talking to me...

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.070
It has to be because I've gotten stronger!

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.570
Since then, every time I fight, I feel it.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.710
A sensation like the cards 
are drawn towards me.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:33.600
And then everything goes my way...

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.810
Miwa complimented me...

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:40.510
I bet Kai will, too...

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.780
If I keep fighting like this, I'm 
sure I'll get even stronger...

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:56.220
And then Kai will be willing to fight me.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.330
I'll do my best!

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.170
But he said something strange...

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.380
That the cards were talking 
to him or something...

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.170
Vanguard Championship
Third Kanto Region Tournament

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:24.170
Return to Regionals

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.630
I think people are glaring at us...

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:37.980
Of course they are! We're the champions 
of the last regional tournament!

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.000
Then they want to take us down...

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:43.340
I-I see...

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:47.380
From the looks of it, victory isn't 
in the cards for Team Q4 this time.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:53.680
Gouki!

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.570
That's right! I forgot about Team Handsome!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.150
Which means, somewhere around here...

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.780
Kamui!!

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.520
Oh, no, you don't!

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.650
I've missed you, Kamui!!

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:17.000
I haven't missed you at all!

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:17.690
How can you say that?!

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.770
Nagisa is so adorable!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.920
Nagisa and Gouki haven't changed...

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.500
I'm not gonna let that remark pass.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.450
If you think we're the same as before, 
you've got another thing coming!

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:36.180
In order to defeat Team Q4,

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.550
everyone in Team Handsome

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:43.430
has gone through a strict training regimen.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.950
So thinking of us as the old Team 
Handsome would be a big mistake!

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:54.200
W-Well, we also went through 
a training camp to brush up.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.790
In fact, it would be unnatural to expect the 
other teams to not do any special training, right?

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.030
Well...

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.480
You're probably right.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.390
Y-Yeah...

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:07.080
Tell me, Kamui. I've changed, right?

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.240
Changed how?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.000
I'm a <i>lot</i> stronger than the 
last time I fought, too!

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:16.070
You oughta take notice when something's 
different about the girl you love!

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:19.530
I don't love you!

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:22.270
Is this the mouth that's 
afraid to tell the truth?!

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.440
What are you lookin' at?

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.950
Kamui belongs to Nagisa!

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.380
You're not gettin' him!

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.770
You're still stuck on that?

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:38.420
Anyway, we're going to put our pride on the 
line as champions of the tournament before last

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.540
and defeat you, Q4!

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.340
We're not going to lose either!

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:47.160
We have unfinished business 
at the national tournament!

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.560
Let's meet at the finals!

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:51.660
Yes!

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.200
Q4...

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.720
Vanguard Championship
Third Kanto Region Tournament...

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.660
is about to begin!

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.770
There are sixteen teams in this tournament.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:14.390
But only one team will make it to the end, 
and get a ticket to the national tournament!

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:18.910
I'm looking forward to 
fights with no regrets!

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.710
Hey, Aichi!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:26.220
Q4 Fight!
by the Mighty Morikawa and His Disciples

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.230
I came all the way here to cheer you on,

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:28.870
so you'd better win or else!

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.780
This is embarrassing...

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.440
Morikawa...

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:37.120
Lose-umi! How dare you 
embarrass Miss Emi like that!

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:47.160
The Vanguard championship official idols,

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.810
Ultra-rare, are going to treat us to a song!

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:53.640
This is the debut of their second 
single, "Stand Up Dream"!

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:51.520
A new song?!

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.750
Kourin!

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:58.940
Just one more step has to be taken.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.370
You still haven't forgotten

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:07.900
The taste of choked-back tears.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.670
Even while being silly on the way home,

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.090
There's a burning deep in your eyes.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:20.780
And it's so bright...

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:27.630
But you might be the only 
one to not notice it.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:30.930
Goddess!

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.490
ViVa Ultra-rare
Kourin Love

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.490
Kourin!

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.740
Have you ever wanted to 
break up with a friend?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:50.810
I'll always cheer you on!

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:02.110
That was Ultra-rare with "Stand Up Dream"!

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.860
Thank you, Ultra-rare!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.550
Kourin! Encore!

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.920
As always, he totally misreads his surroundings...

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.150
MS, yo!

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.790
Okay, let's go!

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.040
Let's imagine!

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.590
Let's Vanguard!

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.550
That was fun!

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:28.000
Hey, Suiko, I thought we were only 
supposed to do that one song as idols...

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:33.120
Oh, it's fine! This way, we're 
able to go to more tournaments.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.560
That's right!

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.780
Let's go watch the fights.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.200
Sure!

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:44.040
Why do we have to go to these regional 
tournaments in the first place?!

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.870
After all, he's not the one, right?

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:50.510
There's one more kid I've got my eye on.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:54.150
Her?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.300
I get a strong vibe off of her.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.980
You think she has the "ability"?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.870
A girl this time, huh?

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.640
<i>She</i> has the ability?

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:24.880
We've begun at last!

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:28.840
The Vanguard Championship
Third Kanto Region Tournament!

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:34.680
This is the climax of 24 hours a day, 365 
days a year of tension! <i>Who's</i> going to win?!

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.870
I'm your old pal, MC Miya!

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.790
And with me to provide color commentary...

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.370
The one who loves Vanguard more 
than three square meals a day!

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.100
The one who didn't have his fill of 
commentating at the national tournament,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.970
so he's here to do the same at regionals,

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.860
Dr. O, <i>oh</i> so happy to be at your service!

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.560
The first fight of the first round

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:56.970
will feature Team Handsome, the team that 
choked back tears in the finals last time around!

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:59.480
Kamui!

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.820
I'll do my best!

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:10.310
Vanguard Championship Third Kanto Region Tournament
Team Stud vs Team Handsome

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:12.550
It's the first fight! Let's Vanguard!

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.480
Rei Watashiki vs Nagisa Daimonji

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.500
Start the first match!

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:26.540
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.060
It's begun at last!

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.850
Yep. Let's do our best, Kamui.

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:41.670
You know it!

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:45.400
A mane of courage! A roar for justice!

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.480
Nagisa the Great rides...

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.510
King of Lions, Lion Heat!

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.330
"Nagisa the Great rides"...

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:57.310
Yeesh...

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.570
The power of love is infinite!

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:04.040
I attack with Lion Heat, 
boosted by Shining Lady!

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.470
That isn't beautiful!

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:17.660
The winner of the first 
match, Nagisa Daimonji!

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:22.670
Kamui, our love won the match!

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:23.880
Leave me alone...

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:30.260
Basskirk Soulblast!

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:35.250
Warriors, be resurrected in 
the name of the Demon King!

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.840
I call two Commodore Blueblood

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.960
and two Dandy Guy, Romario

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.870
to the Rear-guard Circle!

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.880
Arcanum! Supreme Annihilation, Resurrection Hell!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:55.150
The winner of the second 
match: Gouki Daimonji!

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.710
That was a fast victory for Team Handsome!

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:01.010
Displaying that overwhelming 
strength we saw last time,

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:03.330
our last runner-up has 
leapt their first hurdle.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.380
Gouki and the rest have gotten even stronger!

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.720
Yeah. They dominated their 
matches and made no errors.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:15.350
If we get to the finals, I bet we'll 
be up against Gouki and his crew.

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:16.400
It's okay.

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.400
We're going to win.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:25.170
Did I say something strange?

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.790
N-No! You're right!

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.640
Yeah! Let's win!

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:34.870
That's the first time I've ever 
heard him say he'll win...

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:01.880
More frustration than you can imagine,

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.640
Holding out against an entangled heart.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.560
A slightly chaotic situation,

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:10.420
So lost that you might quit.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:15.750
Flipping over inside your head,

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:20.760
Imagine the you

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:26.500
Of tomorrow, yeah!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:32.420
From now, the matches will take you 
to a future you wanna get through.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.050
Team Cheerleader vs Team Gymnast

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:38.660
Don't give up! There's a place on the 
other side that you can't see yet.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:44.340
Believe that there is something in the match.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:46.820
We don't need any reasons or excuses.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:53.660
We're seeing a lot of passion in the second 
and third fights of the first round!

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:57.580
However, the more powerful teams 
aren't necessarily the ones winning!

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:02.870
Teams that are here for the first time are 
advancing at the same rate as more experienced teams.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.810
The world of Vanguard fights 
is one of rapid progress.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:11.390
It's possible that the pattern you used 
to win yesterday won't work tomorrow.

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:15.840
That's what makes Vanguard 
fights <i>oh</i> so interesting!

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.040
Are you excited?!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.090
I am indeed!

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:23.230
It looks like the bar's 
been raised this time.

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:24.820
You think so?

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.410
Well, it doesn't matter. I'm gonna win!

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:30.840
I don't care who's here. 
I'm not going to lose!

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:40.160
I'm doing a final check of the 
deck I'm going to fight with.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.980
I heard the voice of the card...

00:16:56.490 --> 00:17:00.790
I see. I'll win if you're with me.

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:06.940
Kai...?

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:16.900
Kai's taking an interest in me.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:20.240
Even though he's never 
looked at my deck before...

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:25.210
Maybe Kai is starting to believe in me...

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.480
I've gotta get stronger!

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:33.900
An unbelievable defeat from a team 
that had a lot of buzz behind it,

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:38.500
a winning streak, joy and sorrow, all of 
these are facets of life that we've seen here.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.930
That's what Vanguard is all about, isn't it?

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:43.810
It's almost our turn...

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:46.850
Let's decide who's going 
to be in the first fight.

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.070
Who'll do the first match...?

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.370
Brother Aichi?!

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:58.570
Can... Can I go first?

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:02.310
I really feel like I can 
win if I fight right now.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.700
No good?

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.810
N-No, Brother!

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:16.240
For a shy guy like you, Brother, 
to say he wants to get out there,

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.920
I'm deeply moved!

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:20.140
By all means, go first!

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:22.070
Right?! Everyone's on board with that, yeah?

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:27.220
Maybe all the training he's done 
has given him confidence...

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.470
That's fine with me.

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:31.570
I have no objections.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:35.620
Then you're our first fighter, Aichi.

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:36.520
Right!

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:39.310
That leaves the second and third matches...

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.630
I'm gonna fight!

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:42.100
Nobody's got any complaints, do they?

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.280
Nope. I'm gonna sit this one out.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:46.510
Kai...?

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:50.370
There should be no problem if I 
don't fight in the first round.

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:53.180
Tch! Trying to look cool again...

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.090
Then I'll go last!

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:57.010
I'll be second, then.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:01.340
I'm tellin' you now, you're not gonna get 
the chance to fight in this tournament!

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:03.970
Good. That's what I'm hoping for.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.510
Every time he opens his 
mouth, it ticks me off!

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:11.330
Has he really gotten stronger? Or...?

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:16.130
Is Kai counting on me...?

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:19.980
Then maybe that means he 
recognizes my skill...

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.180
Let's do our best, Kamui and Misaki!

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:25.940
Right!

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.790
Leave it to me!

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:34.970
Team Fragrance vs Team Q4

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.540
Thank you for your patience!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:38.170
Here come the champions of the last regional 
tournament, Team Quadrifolio, Q4!

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.460
Yeah! There they are!

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:43.460
We've been waiting for you!

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:45.580
The headliners are here!

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.430
Aichi!

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:50.220
Get 'em, Kamui the Great!

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:51.960
GE, yo!

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:54.990
And facing off against Q4 is...

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.250
Team Fragrance!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.600
While a new team, they've proven their talent

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:03.920
by advancing in their shop tournament 
with overwhelming force!

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:07.100
In the end, which team will be victorious?!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.010
It's a shame,

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:15.070
but Q4 is going to be out in the first round.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:18.260
Excuse me?! You don't know 
what you're talkin' about!

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:20.210
Sayin' things that are brownless...!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:21.550
Groundless...

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.530
Don't get so worked up.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:28.760
I can smell that from here!

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:29.880
Is that a flower?

00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:31.690
Lavender...

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:37.050
That's right. The scent of lavender 
has a calming effect on the emotions.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:39.100
We're perfumers.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:41.250
Performers...?

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:42.900
Perfumers...

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.480
That's why you have perfume...

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:47.320
We're scent specialists.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:50.130
We can analyze and reproduce any aroma.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:53.570
You know that people also have scents, right?

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:59.390
And that scent changes according to the 
person's emotions: happiness, sadness or anger.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:01.100
You mean...

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:05.470
That's right. It's impossible 
to hide your feelings from us.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.630
If the opponent is agitated, we attack.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:11.360
If their spirit is strong, 
we go on the defensive.

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:14.460
Do you really think you can beat us?

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:15.860
There's no way!

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:18.880
They're persuasive...

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:21.380
There's fear mixed in with your scent.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:23.570
Th-That's baloney!

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:26.870
That's a great talent.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:30.670
But... we're going to win!

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.890
Brother Aichi, that was cool!

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.120
He's totally motivated!

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:43.580
Of course! He's my disciple!

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.380
Good luck, Aichi!

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:47.000
The Great Kamui!

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.760
GK, yo!

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:51.380
Then I'll cheer, "Misaki, go for it!"

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.190
I feel it...

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:57.450
You're nervous, aren't you?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:00.450
Will you really be able to win like that?

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:15.880
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:53.770
The regional Vanguard 
championship tournament...

00:23:53.770 --> 00:23:55.970
The regional tournament is here!

00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:57.970
For me, it's merely a checkpoint,

00:23:57.970 --> 00:24:00.490
but it's a major step for you, Aichi!

00:24:00.490 --> 00:24:01.490
You never change...

00:24:01.490 --> 00:24:04.270
Come on! I went to all this trouble 
making a banner, so help me!

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:04.930
Fine!

00:24:04.930 --> 00:24:06.630
Uh, which side is the front?

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:08.330
Next time: Dangerous Scent!

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:10.200
Everyone, thank you for your support!

00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:12.970
I have a much better image 
now than when I started!

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:15.550
There, there! You'll make it to 
the final round nice and smoothly!

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.860
I feel like I've seen that opponent before...
